    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Describing symptoms",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something hurts, use Jeg har vondt i …, literally «I have pain in …». Unlike English «my head hurts», Norwegian uses «I have» here.",
      "Syk means «ill» and forkjølet means «having a cold». Legevakt is the medical centre that deals with urgent cases outside normal hours; it does not mean «pharmacy»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
